fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.17123056523858304,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.3069173739058382,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0009868623943748843,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":98.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.008590001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":5.7,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Hess Midstream LP acquires, owns, operates, and develops midstream assets and provide fee-based services to sponsor, its subsidiaries, and third-party customers in the United States. It operates through three segments: Gathering; Processing and Storage; and Terminaling and Export. The Gathering segment owns natural gas gathering and compression systems; crude oil gathering systems; and produced water gathering and disposal facilities. Its gathering system consists of approximately 1,430 miles of high- and low-pressure natural gas and natural gas liquids gathering pipelines with capacity of approximately 685 million cubic feet per day; crude oil gathering system comprises approximately 615 miles of crude oil gathering pipelines; and produces water gathering system that includes approximately 360 miles of pipelines in gathering systems. The Processing and Storage segment comprises Tioga Gas Plant, a natural gas processing and fractionation plant located in Tioga, North Dakota; Mentor Storage Terminal, a propane storage cavern and rail, and truck loading and unloading facility located in Mentor, Minnesota; and Terminaling and Export segment that owns Ramberg terminal facility, the Tioga rail terminal, crude oil rail cars, and other Dakota access pipeline connections, as well as Johnson's Corner Header System, a crude oil pipeline header system; and other DAPL connections. Hess Midstream LP was formerly known as Hess Midstream Partners LP and changed its name to Hess Midstream LP in December 2019. Hess Midstream LP was founded in 2014 and is based in Houston, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jonathan C. Stein | Chief Executive Officer of Hess Midstream GP LLC | Age 56","financial_summary":["Hess Midstream LP is a mid-cap energy business with a $6.2B market cap on $1.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +3.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","The business throws off $728M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 45 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.79\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -14.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn.","Management returns a meaningful 17.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 5.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 47% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 19% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Hess Midstream Partners LP (NYSE:HESM) Sees Significant Increase in Short Interest","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/hess-midstream-partners-lp-nysehesm-sees-significant-increase-in-short-interest.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793629277.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.974,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Hess Midstream (HESM) Just Gave Investors Something To Think About","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-hesm/hess-midstream/news/hess-midstream-hesm-just-gave-investors-something-to-think-a","date":"2026-11-02"